// The standard types, by name. Each is one cell of stdty; the literal index
// is what tells these functions apart under id's duplicate-logic rule, which
// is also why a single ty_std(i) does not exist -- the call sites would then
// carry the magic numbers instead.

ty_int() {
} return int (import stdty)[0];

ty_uint() {
} return int (import stdty)[1];

ty_long() {
} return int (import stdty)[2];
